title: University content mapped to Paradigm concept symbols
summary: Created .purpose files for university course content (49 lessons across 5 courses) and PLSAT exam content (20 question groups), mapping each to the Paradigm concept symbols they teach or test. Added university-content-sync habit to warn at postflight when modified features have university content that may need updating. Ripple analysis now surfaces affected lessons and PLSAT questions when any mapped concept changes.
symbols_touched:
  - '#university-courses'
  - '#plsat-v3'
  - '#plsat-v2'
files_created:
  - packages/university/src/content/courses/.purpose
  - packages/university/src/content/plsat/.purpose
  - .paradigm/habits/university-content-sync.habit
decisions:
  - id: D-lesson-as-component
    decision: Map each university lesson as a component in .purpose with references to concept symbols
    rationale: 'Makes ripple analysis work natively — changing #lore-system shows which lessons and PLSAT groups are affected without any custom tooling.'
  - id: D-plsat-by-concept-group
    decision: Group PLSAT questions by concept rather than individual slots
    rationale: 99 individual slot entries would be unwieldy. Grouping by concept (symbol-system, portal-protocol, etc.) provides useful granularity without bloat.
  - id: D-habit-warn-not-block
    decision: Set university-content-sync habit to warn severity, not block
    rationale: Not every feature change requires university updates. Warn surfaces the connection; blocking would create false positives.
learnings:
  - 'Component references in .purpose files must quote # symbols to avoid YAML comment parsing'
  - Ripple fallback grep search catches .purpose references even for concept symbols not in the main index
  - Reindex after adding .purpose files causes 3 university-related protocols to go stale (exemplar dirs changed)
tags:
  - arc:expansion-plan
